Description: the libmagic 5.17 bundled in ext/fileinfo (finfo_file(), finfo_buffer(), mime_content_type() on uploaded files): the number of elements of a CDF vector (Office documents) without a limit (CVE-2019-18218: no overflow in the copy of PHP, but memory without a bound), and the fixes of file 5.30 and 5.31 for crafted files found by OSS-Fuzz: a read past the buffer when comparing with compacted whitespace (softmagic.c), PR/599, a read past the end of a CDF string vector, is_tar() rewritten without signed counters and a strcmp() of an unterminated field, the property info of a bad CDF freed and its pointer cleared on the error (a double free of its callers), a field that could not be read set to 0, the sectors of a CDF limited further
Origin: Debian php5 5.6.40+dfsg-0+deb8u12 (jessie LTS and its ELTS), debian/patches/not-cve-but-bug-CVE-2019-18218.patch (the limit of file 5.38, Christos Zoulas, PHP 7.2.24); file commits FILE5_30-12-g77a7041f, FILE5_30-18-g4e4e7609, FILE5_30-19-g7605984c, FILE5_30-30-gc703aa9f, FILE5_30-38-gfd42e119, FILE5_30-39-geb973428 (Christos Zoulas, March and April 2017), as Debian carries them on file 5.30 (1:5.30-1+deb9u3, stretch LTS and its ELTS), the paths src/ as ext/fileinfo/libmagic/ and the free of the error path of cdf_read_property_info() on the code of 5.17, which frees there already

